# doctor.crontab.txt — FULL MERGED crontab: the LIVE deadline sweeps + 18:00 guardian
# (UNCHANGED, copied verbatim from crontab.proposed.txt) PLUS the additive "Ecom Doctor"
# self-healing watchdog lines (daily 18:30 / weekly Sun 19:00 / monthly 1st 19:30 IST).
#
# This is the ONE file the LEAD installs in a single shot:   crontab tools/cron/doctor.crontab.txt
# (Installation is the LEAD's call after W3 PASS — W3 only proposes. The doctor section is
#  ADDITIVE: the sweep + guardian lines below are byte-for-byte the live crontab; nothing
#  about the live pipeline changes. setup_cron.sh only touches "# ecom-intel"-tagged lines,
#  so it stays re-runnable over this file.)
# Cron runs in system-local time = IST (the live `0 18` guardian is 18:00 IST — confirmed).
# ============================ LIVE SWEEPS + GUARDIAN (UNCHANGED) ============================
# Model: cron fires tools/cron/deadline_sweep.sh <slot> EARLY (00:30 tick). The
# script predicts the serial chain's runtime from history (predict_lead.py), sleeps
# until <slot> - predicted_lead (LEAD_MAX caps the lead so the START never drifts
# earlier than ~01:02 IST — the proven timing that lets the Mac-fed q-commerce
# spools land), runs ./run_all.sh with DEFER_DELIVERY=1, and send_batch.py holds
# every platform's report and delivers them as ONE batch AT the slot time ("everyone
# comes at the timing, not starts at it"). If the chain overruns, the batch goes
# out as soon as it's done, marked "(late by Xm)".

# 10:00 IST slot — fire 00:30; LEAD_MAX=32400 pins the chain START to ~01:02 IST (the
# SAME proven start as the old 12:00 batch), so the Mac-fed q-commerce spools land
# exactly as before — only the batch RELEASE moves 12:00 -> 10:00 (goal #60, 2026-07-03).
# SWEEP_SITES=0 disables the 3 availability-site auto-redeploys (owner 2026-07-04, goal #61):
# only jivo-pincode-app.vercel.app is refreshed daily now (its own data-bank hook ~07:00 + 16:30 cron).
30 0 * * * cd /opt/ecom-intel && SWEEP_SITES=0 LEAD_MAX=32400 COVERAGE_DAILY=1 ./tools/cron/deadline_sweep.sh 10:00 >> logs/cron.log 2>&1   # ecom-intel deadline-batch 10:00
*/20 0-9 * * * cd /opt/ecom-intel && ./tools/cron/sweep_watchdog.sh 10:00 >> logs/sweep_watchdog.cron.log 2>&1   # 10:00-sweep catch-up watchdog (guards the single 00:30 launch tick — 2026-07-01 fix)
# 15:00 IST slot — fire 11:30, same mechanics, batch lands AT 15:00.
# 18:00 IST daily guardian deep-dive — UNCHANGED from the live crontab (read-only
# 11-bug-class audit + trend; Telegram-alerts only on a NEW bug class vs yesterday).
0 18 * * * cd /opt/ecom-intel && ./tools/guardian_daily.sh >> logs/guardian.log 2>&1   # ecom-intel guardian-daily (paused w/ sweeps; un-pause together)
# ================================ ECOM DOCTOR (ADDITIVE) ====================================
# Self-healing watchdog. After BOTH daily sweeps have landed (12:00 + 15:00) and the 18:00
# guardian deep-dive has run, the doctor gathers deterministic health signals
# (tools/cron/health_snapshot.py) and — ONLY if something is wrong — invokes a bounded headless
# Claude agent (tools/cron/doctor_prompt.md + the vetted tools/cron/safe_fixes/ menu) to
# diagnose, auto-apply a VETTED-SAFE fix or PROPOSE-only, and ALWAYS alert the owner. It never
# pushes, only runs when ECOM_DOCTOR_ENABLE=1 (kill switch = unset it in secrets.env), and is
# flock-guarded so two doctors never overlap. A doctor crash can NEVER touch the sweeps above.
# WHY 18:30 daily: it must see the WHOLE day — both sweep batches (15:00 + its post-batch tail
# done ~15:01) AND the 18:00 guardian's fresh health-<date>.md. 18:30 is the first slot strictly
# after the guardian finishes (guardian is read-only/seconds), so the doctor reads the complete,
# settled signal set. The headline signal it exists to catch — a platform HELD N sweeps in a row
# (the 2-day silent flipkart/zepto false-positive hold) — is only fully visible once both of the
# day's sweeps are in reviews/.
30 18 * * * cd /opt/ecom-intel && ./tools/cron/doctor.sh daily >> logs/doctor.log 2>&1   # ecom-intel doctor-daily
# WHY Sunday 19:00 weekly: a 7-day trend pass (held-platform frequency, recurring SUSPECT
# reasons, prediction-vs-actual drift, coverage trends) — runs after Sunday's daily doctor
# (18:30) so it never races it; 30m apart, both are short unless the agent is invoked (lock
# serializes that anyway).
0 19 * * 0 cd /opt/ecom-intel && ./tools/cron/doctor.sh weekly >> logs/doctor.log 2>&1   # ecom-intel doctor-weekly
# WHY 1st 19:30 monthly: a 30-day rollup — runs after the daily (18:30) and (when the 1st is a
# Sunday) after the weekly (19:00), each 30m apart and lock-serialized so they never overlap.
30 19 1 * * cd /opt/ecom-intel && ./tools/cron/doctor.sh monthly >> logs/doctor.log 2>&1   # ecom-intel doctor-monthly
# ===========================================================================================
# OVERLAP / SAFETY NOTES (doctor lines)
# - The three doctor lines are mutually exclusive in practice (18:30 / 19:00 / 19:30, ≥30m
#   apart) and additionally serialized by logs/.doctor.lock (flock -n in doctor.sh) — a long
#   agent run from the daily can never be clobbered by the weekly/monthly; the later one logs
#   "another doctor holds the lock" and exits.
# - All three run in the EVENING (18:30–19:30), well clear of the single sweep chain
#   (~01:02 start, batch spooled ~02:53, downstream done ~07:31, released AT 10:00) and the
#   18:00 guardian (read-only, seconds). No sweep/guardian overlap by construction.
# - The doctor reads artifacts only and (when it acts) calls vetted safe_fixes/ scripts that are
#   themselves lock-guarded (sweep-chain / amazon-account / .heal-<p>) and refuse during a live
#   sweep window — so even a safe-fix re-run can't collide with a sweep.
# - doctor.sh is fully fail-safe: if ECOM_DOCTOR_ENABLE!=1 it no-ops; any internal error still
#   fires an owner alert and exits 0; it has no path that can abort or modify the sweep crons.
# Dropped vs the live crontab: nothing. This file is the live crontab + the 3 doctor lines.
10 10 * * * cd /opt/ecom-intel && python3 tools/cron/check_layout.py >> logs/layout_gate.log 2>&1   # ecom-intel layout gate (post 10:00 batch)
# Telegram-alerts the owner on any failure. Built 2026-06-11.
0 10 * * * cd /opt/ecom-intel && /usr/bin/tmux new-session -d -s "mailgw-am-$(date +\%Y\%m\%d)" './tools/mailer/mail_price_data.sh am'   # ecom-mailer price-data am
30 5 * * * /root/jivo-factory-intel/bin/factory_refresh.sh >> /root/jivo-factory-intel/daily.log 2>&1   # jivo-factory daily source refresh (05:30 IST; feeds event-driven data-bank fusion after noon)
# >>> jivo-intel source-refresh feeder (managed by Claude 2026-06-30; owner authorized .env auto-refresh) >>>
# Refresh the JIVO app (ecom.jivo.in) source vault before same-day event-driven data-bank fusion.
# auth.sh re-logins daily using creds in /root/jivo-intel/.env (0600, gitignored). Fail-closed:
# any failure does NOT commit and alerts; source-only. Data-bank fusion is event-driven after the noon
# ecom/competitor chain, not a fixed 06:00 cron.
CRON_TZ=Asia/Kolkata
